class:: SpectralBasisOsc
summary:: Wavetable synthesis from shaped orthogonal-basis coefficients
categories:: UGens>Generators>Deterministic
related:: Guides/NovelOscillators

description::

SpectralBasisOsc builds a periodic waveform from a deterministic coefficient
envelope. Fourier, Walsh, Haar, and Daubechies-4 inverse transforms turn the
same envelope into distinct timbral families.

Two internal table banks are allocated at initialization. Parameter changes
regenerate the inactive bank only at calculation-block boundaries, subject to
code::refresh::. DC is removed, the table is peak-normalized, mip levels are
generated, and playback crossfades to the new bank over approximately 20
milliseconds. No FFT plan or memory allocation occurs in the calculation
callback.

The closest vanilla UGen is link::Classes/Osc::. Both play a periodic
wavetable, but SpectralBasisOsc constructs and refreshes its own mipmapped
tables from alternative transform bases.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: freq
Signed playback frequency in hertz.

argument:: basis
Transform selection, rounded and clamped to code::0..3::. The meanings are
code::0:: Fourier, code::1:: Walsh, code::2:: Haar, and code::3::
Daubechies-4.

argument:: center
Center of the coefficient envelope from code::0:: through code::1::.

argument:: width
Envelope width, clamped to code::0.005..1::.

argument:: tilt
Exponential spectral tilt, clamped to code::-8..8::.

argument:: skew
Asymmetry of the two envelope sides, clamped to code::-0.95..0.95::.

argument:: phase
Readout phase offset in radians.

argument:: refresh
Maximum table regenerations per second, clamped to code::0.1..200::.

argument:: tableSize
Initialization-rate power of two from code::128:: through code::4096::. Larger
tables improve waveform resolution but increase per-instance memory and
regeneration cost.

argument:: mul
Output multiplier.

argument:: add
Offset added after multiplication.

returns::
A mono audio-rate signal.

method:: kr

SpectralBasisOsc is audio-rate only. This method throws an error.

subsection:: Discussion

Identical controls produce identical tables; the UGen has no hidden random
phase. Playback begins with a fully generated table, so it has no silent
warmup. Fast control changes are refresh-limited, and a new regeneration waits
until the current table crossfade completes.

examples::

code::
(
{ SpectralBasisOsc.ar(90, 0, 0.2, 0.12) * 0.075 }.play;
)
::

code::
(
{
    var center = LFTri.kr(0.05).range(0.05, 0.9);
    var width = LFNoise1.kr(0.2).range(0.03, 0.3);
    SpectralBasisOsc.ar(
        55, basis: 3, center: center, width: width,
        tilt: -0.4,
        skew: LFNoise1.kr(0.13).range(-0.8, 0.8),
        refresh: 40, tableSize: 1024
    ) * 0.06
}.play;
)
::

